From 4f27c98b8d1fbf575da2508a4b7b7a615e7583f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Grasso <me@leonardograsso.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:01:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mermaid-text): leave sequence block frames unshaded

Block frames filled their interior with U+2591 after drawing, so the spaces between words of labels and messages inside a block became shade cells, which terminals draw as grey bands that break the text. Frame interiors now stay blank; rect blocks keep their shade.
---
 crates/mermaid-text/CHANGELOG.md              |  4 ++
 crates/mermaid-text/src/render/sequence.rs    | 46 +++-----------
 crates/mermaid-text/tests/snapshots.rs        | 63 +++++--------------
 .../snapshots__rect_nested_inside_loop.snap   |  8 +--
 ...apshots__sequence_with_alt_else_block.snap | 12 ++--
 .../snapshots__sequence_with_loop_block.snap  |  6 +-
 ...pshots__sequence_with_nested_loop_alt.snap | 16 ++---
 .../snapshots__sequence_with_opt_block.snap   |  6 +-
 ...sequence_with_par_and_critical_blocks.snap | 24 +++----
 9 files changed, 63 insertions(+), 122 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/mermaid-text/CHANGELOG.md b/crates/mermaid-text/CHANGELOG.md
index 7e689b2..76796f0 100644
--- a/crates/mermaid-text/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/mermaid-text/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -20,6 +20,10 @@ This project adheres to [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/)
 
 ### Changed
 
+- Sequence block frames (`loop`, `alt`, `opt`, `par`, `critical`, `break`)
+  no longer fill their interior with `░`: in terminals the shade reads as
+  grey bands that break the text of labels and messages inside. `rect`
+  blocks keep their shade.
 - `tests/strict_max_width.rs` uses a class diagram as its fixed-width
   fixture, since sequence diagrams now fit the budget.
 
